# Follow-up to 2026-09-28-14.play: the good-style shaman:restoration pull on
# flags read hero=0/dead from fightTime~14s through 45s across three chained
# play calls, never reviving. direction.md's Tried and dropped section says
# chained play() calls can miss a real revival between samples -- only a
# single play call followed by bare wait/state polling settles whether this
# is a real stall or the known artifact. Same cell, same fresh save (pull 1
# is deterministic), one short play call to reach the same death, then pure
# wait/state after.
open
tap battleground
tap map:flags
tap class:shaman:restoration
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15

play good 20
state
shot died

wait 5
state
shot plus5

wait 5
state
shot plus10

wait 10
state
shot plus20

wait 15
state
shot plus35
